WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.147
Time zones are easier when you separate the instant from its display.

00:00:04.147 --> 00:00:07.377
A timestamptz represents an instant.

00:00:07.377 --> 00:00:12.012
That instant can be displayed using Eastern time, UTC, or another zone.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:18.012
The clock reading changes, but the underlying instant does not.

00:00:18.012 --> 00:00:21.732
This distinction is essential for logs, orders, and events collected across locations.

00:00:21.732 --> 00:00:30.437
Time zones matter whenever events from different locations need to be compared on one timeline.

00:00:30.437 --> 00:00:38.102
Store instants in a consistent form, often using TIMESTAMPTZ, and convert to local time for presentation.

00:00:38.102 --> 00:00:43.579
Do not permanently rewrite an instant just because a report needs to display it in a local zone.
